Z||000000||underdog||06-02-2001||12:36 PM||||how hard is it to do this? can i use my existing tranny? for the people who have done this can you give me a few pointers and tips. i want to do it cheap, i know i can get the engine, but i was wondering what other costs there were<P>thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||gabriel||06-02-2001||01:49 PM||||&gt;i want to do it cheap, <P> Everytime I read cheap in the same sentence as engine swap, I cringe.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>&gt;can i use my existing tranny? <P>It might help if we knew what that tranny is ... but using a manual raises a whole new crop of issues.  Also what Series/year engine you are talking about ... <P> To start, try a search under 3800SC, there's lots of info, then return & ask more questions.<P>The issues are cradle mods, axles, wiring harness splicing, shifter mods, & exhaust systems. - Assuming you go with the AOD trans that came with your particular engine.<P> If you go with a manual, then there are more issues, depending on the PCM.<P>  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||06-02-2001||02:14 PM||||you're not going to get much done under $3000 and that's a bare minimum. $5000 to 7000 is a more realistic figure.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||06-02-2001||03:21 PM||||5K seems about right. 3K will not include angle-iron and hockey pucks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I've decided to go the same route, vs. a 3.4TDC, as the TDC, while an easier fit will cost more to have reconditioned (and MUCH harder to find up here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">). The s-II SC is fairly common, in comparison: 3 or 4 cars that I can think of off-hand have 'em, VS. the one that I know of with the 3.4TDC.<BR>Realistically, I'm sure that I could nickle and dime my way to a 2-3k swap, but I'd rather have it done right, and not have to worry about it. Therefore, I'm saving my pennies for now, and will do it next year (I hope). Good luck, whatever you do, but remember that the $100 you didn't spend today will probably bite you in the ass tommorrow. And bring it's Friends and Relations.||||reg||4
Z||000004||Philphine||06-02-2001||08:17 PM||||if you only know of one car i'm guessing it's the lumina. if so, you can also find them in similar year cutlasses and grand prix'. i would't dought that it's probaly in a buick too. never noticed one though.||||reg||1
